   "body": "The Autoware Tutorial & Workshop recordings from IEEE IV 2026 are now available to watch on demand. Recorded in Detroit on June 22, 2026, this collection brings together an introduction, three tutorials, eight workshop sessions and a poster session . Explore Autoware fundamentals, discover research and applications, and revisit the sessions at your own pace. Watch the full playlist → Autoware Tutorial & Workshop | IEEE IV 2026 Start here: Introduction Start with the opening welcome, including remarks from Autoware Foundation Board member Christian John . You can also revisit highlights from Detroit in our recap video. Tutorials Explore the Autoware pipeline and applications spanning simulation, off-road autonomy and vehicle integration. Workshops Discover research, technical developments and applications shared by the Autoware community at IEEE IV 2026. Poster Session Explore the workshop’s 12 accepted research papers through one-minute lightning talks from the Autoware community. Thank you to our speakers, organizers ( Alexander Carballo | Simon Thompson ) and participants for contributing to this knowledge-sharing community event and helping advance open-source autonomous driving. We look forward to continuing the journey—and seeing the community again at IEEE IV 2027 in Perth, Australia ! Refer to the original event program below: The Autoware Tutorial & Workshop at the IEEE Intelligent Vehicles Symposium (IV 2026) The post Watch on demand: Autoware Tutorial & Workshop at IEEE IV 2026 appeared first on Autoware ."
